TORTURE

This help database exists to break the slug writer.

See also: CAFE
#
CAFE CAFé

An entry whose keywords are not ASCII. © 2001.
#
SLUG COLLISION

HelpSlug joins an entry's keywords with a space, lowercases them and
collapses every non-alphanumeric run to one dash. So this entry and
the next one both slug to "slug-collision", from two different
keyword lines, and the writer has to disambiguate them.
#
SLUG-COLLISION

The second half of the collision above. One of us gets a numeric
suffix on our file name; which one is decided by file order.
#
! ^

A keyword line of pure punctuation, which slugs to the empty string.
The writer falls back to a positional name for this one.
#
LONG

An entry with a body long enough to be worth wrapping, a line that is
deliberately blank in the middle of it:

and a line that ends in trailing whitespace:   
#
$
